# terminal preference order for xdg-terminal-exec, which is what omarchy's
# SUPER+RETURN and the omarchy launcher call. the first entry that resolves to an
# installed desktop file wins.
#
# it names wezterm/desktop/org.wezfurlong.wezterm.desktop, which is our own entry
# rather than the packaged one: ours runs `wezterm connect unix` so opening a
# terminal attaches the layout instead of spawning a bare window beside it.
#
# this lives outside wezterm/ on purpose. it is a system-level choice of terminal,
# not wezterm configuration, and it names a fallback too.
#
# without this file the choice among the installed TerminalEmulator entries is
# unspecified. foot is second so a broken or missing wezterm still leaves a
# working terminal on the keybind; it is foot rather than alacritty because
# omarchy ships foot and no longer ships alacritty.
org.wezfurlong.wezterm.desktop
foot.desktop
